  <h1>Dropwatch Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 18, 2026</p>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Dropwatch collects, uses, stores, and protects information when you use our Discord community, bot, website, and alert services.</p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

  <h3>Discord Information</h3>
  <p>We may collect information provided through Discord that is necessary to operate Dropwatch, including your Discord user ID, username, display name, server membership, roles, and subscription status.</p>

  <h3>Subscription Information</h3>
  <p>If you subscribe to a Premium service, we may process information related to your subscription, including your selected plan, subscription status, billing dates, and transaction status. Payment information may be processed by third-party payment providers, and Dropwatch does not intentionally store complete payment card numbers.</p>

  <h3>Service Usage Information</h3>
  <p>We may collect information about how you use Dropwatch, including alert preferences, notification settings, bot commands, and technical information used to diagnose errors and improve the service.</p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

  <p>We may use collected information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide Dropwatch alerts and services.</li>
    <li>Manage Premium subscriptions and access.</li>
    <li>Send service-related communications.</li>
    <li>Provide customer support.</li>
    <li>Improve the Dropwatch service.</li>
    <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, and unauthorized access.</li>
    <li>Troubleshoot technical problems.</li>
    <li>Comply with applicable legal requirements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Discord</h2>

  <p>Dropwatch operates through Discord. Discord independently processes information according to its own privacy practices and policies. Dropwatch may receive limited information from Discord that is necessary for the bot and community to function.</p>

  <h2>4. Payment Providers</h2>

  <p>Premium subscriptions may use third-party payment providers. Those providers may collect and process payment information according to their own privacy policies and terms.</p>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Websites</h2>

  <p>Dropwatch may provide links to third-party retailers, marketplaces, websites, or services. These third parties have their own privacy policies and terms. Dropwatch is not responsible for the privacy practices of third-party websites.</p>

  <h2>6. Sharing Information</h2>

  <p>Information may be shared with service providers that help operate Dropwatch, including providers for hosting, payments, communications, analytics, monitoring, security, fraud prevention, and customer support.</p>

  <p>Information may also be disclosed when reasonably necessary to comply with legal obligations, respond to lawful requests, protect rights or safety, investigate abuse, or protect the security of the service.</p>

  <h2>7. Sale of Personal Information</h2>

  <p>Dropwatch does not sell personal information as a core part of its business.</p>

  <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>

  <p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the service, maintain subscription records, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes, prevent abuse, and protect the security of Dropwatch.</p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>

  <p>We use reasonable measures designed to protect information from unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. However, no online service can guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>10. Your Rights</h2>

  <p>Depending on applicable law, you may have rights regarding your personal information, including requesting access, correction, deletion, information about processing, or other applicable privacy rights.</p>

  <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>

  <p>Dropwatch is not intended to knowingly collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law. If you believe information has been collected improperly, please contact Dropwatch through its official support channel.</p>

  <h2>12. International Users</h2>

  <p>If you use Dropwatch from outside the United States, your information may be processed or stored in countries where Dropwatch or its service providers operate.</p>

  <h2>13. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The updated version will be posted with a new "Last Updated" date.</p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>

  <p>For privacy questions or requests, please contact Dropwatch through its official support channel.</p>

